  "authority": "Each new acceptor begins with verified old-quorum approval. Canonical input descriptors bind ordered reports, full history counts and digests. Complete old-quorum history replay and bootstrap agreement precede durable acceptance and reopen.",
  "rounds": "Ordered counter/coordinator promises sync before reply. A new quorum selects its highest accepted input. The coordinator binds its own nomination durably before relay, preventing same-round input replacement after restart. Authenticated accepting peers bind that nomination to its coordinator, proposal, round and input.",
  "choice": "A distinct new majority must accept one exact input at one round. The chosen proof pins that input across recovery rounds. These are transition votes; no API exposes a writable application cell, commit acknowledgement or promoted learner.",
  "storage": "Separate exclusive-owner decision store, full-sync state journal, retained complete old authority and bounded atomic WAL batches for input. Exact and overlapping retries preserve logical ordinals; changed prefixes and gaps reject. Referenced missing input cannot be silently recreated; malformed authority/state fails repeated reopen.",
  "trust_model": "Crash faults with authenticated report sources. Node IDs and stored report bytes are not independently verifiable signatures. Peer orchestration must authenticate all report identities before using these constructors and store APIs.",
